  setLiteral(11136, "   modes up to %.0f Hz");
  setLiteral(11137, "stereo panner only");
  setLiteral(11138, "Magenta: the delay echoes as they reach the listener (direct path + echo time) \342\200\223 switch the delay in its section");
  setLiteral(11139, "Free field: no walls \342\200\223 no reverb");
  setLiteral(11140, "Room off \342\200\223 no reverb");
  setLiteral(11141, "63");
  setLiteral(11142, "250");
  setLiteral(11143, "500");
  setLiteral(11144, "2k");
  setLiteral(11145, "4k");
  setLiteral(11146, "Reverb time RT60 per octave band \342\200\223 exactly what the reverb engine plays (walls, materials, air). Green = room modes: below that frequency a small room rings on its own tones");
  setLiteral(11147, "room modes \342\200\223 below %.0f Hz");
  setLiteral(11148, "no room modes (large room)");
  setLiteral(11149, "diffuse reverb");
  setLiteral(11150, "RT60 (mid)");
  setLiteral(11151, "Room volume");
  setLiteral(11152, "%.1f m\302\263");
  setLiteral(11153, "%.0f m\302\263");
  setLiteral(11154, "Mean free path");
  setLiteral(11155, "Modes up to");
  setLiteral(11156, "%.0f Hz");
  setLiteral(11157, "Mean free path = average way of the sound between two reflections; critical distance = where direct sound and room sound are equally loud; modes = the room's own resonances (Schroeder frequency)");
  setLiteral(11158, "R1");
  setLiteral(11159, "R2");
  setLiteral(11160, "Reflectors on / off (both) \342\200\223 the settings stay");
  setLiteral(11161, "R1 / R2: click = this reflector on / off (and select it for the knobs). Two freely placed vertical planes (facade, rock face, fence, hedge) \342\200\223 each one adds a real echo. A dot = on");
  setLiteral(11162, "Material: Facade (brick, stone), Glass, Rock, Fence (reflects little), Hedge (soft) \342\200\223 Off removes the reflector");
  setLiteral(11163, "%+.0f dB");
  setLiteral(11164, "X");
  setLiteral(11165, "Y");
  setLiteral(11166, "Angle");
  setLiteral(11167, "Length");
  setLiteral(11168, "Position of the reflector's center in the free-field area (also: drag its handle in the Stage View)");
  setLiteral(11169, "Direction of the wall line seen from above: 0\302\260 = along the width, 90\302\260 = along the depth");
  setLiteral(11170, "Length of the reflector \342\200\223 the echo only exists where the sound hits it");
  setLiteral(11171, "Level of this echo in dB. 0 = physically exact (a facade 10 m away is 20 dB below the direct sound \342\200\223 hardly audible); +12 = film default, clearly audible; up to +24");
  setLiteral(11172, "Height of the reflector \342\200\223 a low fence reflects only low sound paths");
  setLiteral(11173, "Asphalt");
  setLiteral(11174, "Hard ground (asphalt, concrete): reflects almost everything \342\200\223 a bright, clear second arrival; with a moving source the typical sweeping comb filter");
  setLiteral(11175, "Grass");
  setLiteral(11176, "Grass: absorbs much and the highs most \342\200\223 a weaker, duller reflection, the comb is shallow");
  setLiteral(11177, "Snow");
  setLiteral(11178, "Fresh snow: very soft \342\200\223 only a muffled trace of the ground reflection is left");
  setLiteral(11179, "Goniometer: the output, left against right \342\200\223 a vertical line = mono, a horizontal line = out of phase, a round cloud = wide. Automatic gain: the loudest moment fills the circle");
  setLiteral(11180, "Ground");
  setLiteral(11181, "Hard");
  setLiteral(11182, "Ground reflection outdoors: the sound also arrives via the ground \342\200\223 Hard (asphalt, concrete) reflects almost everything, Grass and Snow absorb much. With a moving source it gives the typical sweeping color of a pass-by");
  setLiteral(11183, "Ahh! \342\200\223 how it works");
  setLiteral(11184, "Signal flow");
  setLiteral(11185, "In \342\206\222 Filter \342\206\222 Source \342\206\222 Delay \342\206\222 Room \342\206\222 Barrier \342\206\222 Out. The strip under the top bar shows the chain: click a module = on / off, Shift+click = solo, hear it alone.");
  setLiteral(11186, "Three views");
  setLiteral(11187, "Basic: film locations as tiles, room, decay, source and barrier at a glance \342\200\223 a hint in the strip shows Expert settings that still change the sound. Expert: the Stage View on top, one module per tab under it ([ and ] = previous / next) \342\200\223 or All = every module at once (key 0). Learn: ten listening tasks that explain what you hear.");
  setLiteral(11188, "Room and positions");
  setLiteral(11189, "Choose a room preset or one of My rooms. Drag source and listener in the plan (Shift+drag = height, 3D shows it; Ctrl/Cmd+drag = only left / right or only forward / back, a dashed line shows it). Reset positions = both back to their start places (listener in the middle, source 2 m in front), the room stays. Loading a room preset keeps source and listener in the same place relative to the room as long as you have not moved them; moved or locked positions stay. Drag the front corner = the room larger or smaller (Ctrl/Cmd = in proportion, Alt = height). Mouse wheel on the floor = zoom the view 0.1 \342\200\246 5x (in and out); the chips Fit and 1:1 fit the whole room / area or go back. With the room off the direct sound still follows the positions (a 3D panner: direction, distance, height), only walls and reverb are gone. Direction (Expert): Src angle and Lis angle dials, or Alt+drag a ball to turn it; Aim = where the source points (Fixed or at the listener), Facing = where the listener looks (Fixed, at the source or along its path). The round arrows next to Aim and Facing reset them; double-click the listener's arrow (or Alt+double-click the source) = the listener looks straight ahead again. Doppler (chip beside Handles): on = a drag glides the pitch like a real move, off = only the distance changes.");
  setLiteral(11190, "Outdoors: no walls, no reverb \342\200\223 only the direct sound, the ground and two reflectors. Ground: Off, Hard, Grass or Snow, its strength with Ground level. Area width and depth = how far source and listener can move. The reflectors R1 and R2 (facade, glass, rock, fence, hedge): drag their dot or panel in the Stage View to move them, Alt+drag turns them, the small square at the panel's end sets the length and, in 3D, the one on the top edge the height; the knobs are in the Reflectors tab, its round button switches both on / off; they keep their place when the area changes. A reflector larger than the view: Fit (or the wheel on the floor, out to 10 %) shows all of it. All reflector values can be automated.");
  setLiteral(11191, "A wall, a window or a door between source and listener: Pos, Size, Height, Open and Damp. The thin line around the room modules marks what belongs to the room.");
  setLiteral(11192, "Delay and tempo");
  setLiteral(11193, "The delay sits before the room \342\200\223 every echo is reverberated too. Tempo tools: tap, listen to the song or use the project tempo; a note value sets the delay at once. A click on Link links or unlinks all.");
  setLiteral(11194, "In and Out = gain before and after the plugin. Dry / wet = the mix. Limiter = a look-ahead peak limiter at -1 dBFS (1.5 ms latency, REAPER compensates it) \342\200\223 a safety net, not a loudness tool. Equal loudness = every room, distance and model plays about as loud as the input, for comparing sounds.");
  setLiteral(11195, "Four ways to keep a sound");
  setLiteral(11196, "A / B = compare quickly while you work (not saved; Match level plays both equally loud). Snapshots 1\342\200\22316 = saved in this project: click = load, Save then a slot = store (a slot in use asks once), right-click = rename / overwrite / clear, keys 1\342\200\2238 and Shift+1\342\200\2238 (Tabs view: Shift+1\342\200\2238 only, 1\342\200\2238 open the tabs, 0 = All); Snapshot Morph blends them and can be automated. Room presets = typical rooms for every project. My rooms = your own rooms, kept on this computer.");
  setLiteral(11197, "Motion (Expert)");
  setLiteral(11198, "Moves the source, the listener or both on a pattern: Circle or Square (around the listener, its own spot or the room center), Left \342\200\223 right, Front \342\200\223 back, Up \342\200\223 down, Wave, a Drawn path (Draw: draw it in the Stage View) or Pass-by (once along a straight line through its own spot, A to B in one cycle time \342\200\223 the status shows the speed in m/s; it starts again with every playback start and loop). Rate in Hz or locked to the tempo (bars and notes), Size in meters, Start = where it begins, Glide = fade in / out. It runs with REAPER's transport, so every playback sounds the same; free-running while stopped. On / off, pattern, rate and size are automatable and stored in snapshots and A / B. The positions are written to the Source / Listener X, Y and height parameters, so REAPER can record the movement as automation (Write or Latch); an envelope in read mode on them overrides the pattern. The Stage View draws the path; Stop on its sign switches it off.");
  setLiteral(11199, "Layout");
  setLiteral(11200, "Drag the edges and corners of the modules and the column divider. Tabs: drag the corner of the module = larger / smaller (double-click = automatic), the bar over the tabs = height of the Stage View, Fit = the module as large as the window allows. Fit all = every module in the window, Lock GUI = the layout stays. V hides the Stage View, the magnifier enlarges a module \342\200\223 or key Z: in Tabs the open module, in All / Fit the module or the Stage View under the mouse (Z again or Esc = back).");
  setLiteral(11201, "Most used keys");
  setLiteral(11202, "1 \342\200\246 9 tabs (Tabs view) or snapshots  \302\267  Ctrl/Cmd+Z undo  \302\267  arrows move the listener  \302\267  [ ] tabs  \302\267  0 Tabs / All  \302\267  Z zoom  \302\267  V Stage View  \302\267  Esc closes  \302\267  hold Ctrl/Cmd = help text under the mouse  \302\267  ? every key");
  setLiteral(11203, "All keys and mouse actions");
  setLiteral(11204, "Read manual");
