  setLiteral(11720, "FREE FIELD  \342\200\223  outdoors, no walls");
  setLiteral(11721, "MOTION  \342\200\223  source or listener on a path");
  setLiteral(11722, "DECAY BY BAND  \342\200\223  reverb time per octave");
  setLiteral(11723, "DELAY  \342\200\223  echoes before the room");
  setLiteral(11724, "REVERB");
  setLiteral(11725, "REFLECTORS  \342\200\223  two free walls outdoors");
  setLiteral(11726, "WALLS");
  setLiteral(11727, "BARRIER");
  setLiteral(11728, "OUTPUT  \342\200\223  levels and limiter");
  setLiteral(11729, "TIMELINE  \342\200\223  the room over time (echogram)");
  setLiteral(11730, "Outdoors: no walls, no ceiling, no reverb \342\200\223 only the direct sound and, with Ground, its");
  setLiteral(11731, "reflection from the floor (Hard = asphalt, Grass, Snow) and the two Reflectors (facade, rock \342\200\246).");
  setLiteral(11732, "Free field on = room off. Presets set area, ground and reflectors. Distance = film perspective.");
  setLiteral(11733, "Moves the source, the listener or both on a pattern: circle, square, left \342\200\223 right, front \342\200\223");
  setLiteral(11734, "back, up \342\200\223 down, wave, a drawn path or a pass-by. Rate in Hz or tempo, Size in m, Glide = the");
  setLiteral(11735, "fade in / out. Runs with the transport \342\200\223 the same place at every playback.");
  setLiteral(11736, "How long the reverb rings in each octave (RT60 = time to fall by 60 dB), exactly as the reverb");
  setLiteral(11737, "engine plays it. Hard walls ring long and bright, soft ones swallow the highs first, air dampens them too.");
  setLiteral(11738, "Green bars: room modes \342\200\223 below this frequency a small room rings on its own tones.");
  setLiteral(11739, "Echoes before the room: L and R each have Time, Feedback (repeats), Level and");
  setLiteral(11740, "a low / high cut in the feedback loop \342\200\223 every repeat gets thinner and darker.");
  setLiteral(11741, "The echoes play into the room, so each one is reverberated. Off = no change.");
  setLiteral(11742, "Room: width, depth, height, Size, absorption, heights and the angle of the source.");
  setLiteral(11743, "Reverb (2nd row): Early / Late level, Decay = RT60, Predelay, Density, Tone and");
  setLiteral(11744, "Reflect = how much all surfaces reflect (100 % = as built). Off = only the source model.");
  setLiteral(11745, "How the room answers: Early = level of the reflections, Late = level of the");
  setLiteral(11746, "reverb, Decay = reverb time RT60, Predelay = gap before the room answers,");
  setLiteral(11747, "Density = smooth or grainy tail, Tone = darker or brighter room sound.");
  setLiteral(11748, "What is making the sound: a phone, a radio, a megaphone \342\200\246 Each model is a");
  setLiteral(11749, "filter curve plus distortion. Drag the points H, 1\342\200\2233 and L to reshape the curve.");
  setLiteral(11750, "Distortion pushes the device. Call line (Expert): band, duplex, codec, dropouts.");
  setLiteral(11751, "Two freely placed vertical planes outdoors: a facade, glass, rock face, fence or hedge.");
  setLiteral(11752, "Each one adds a real echo from where it stands (X, Y, Angle, Length, Height) \342\200\223 the sound");
  setLiteral(11753, "bounces off it like off a house wall. Drag the R1 / R2 handles in the Stage View.");
  setLiteral(11754, "What the room is made of. Choose a surface, then a material: hard materials");
  setLiteral(11755, "(glass, concrete) reflect \342\200\223 long, bright reverb; soft materials (curtain, foam)");
  setLiteral(11756, "absorb \342\200\223 short, dry room. Floor + ceiling switches their reflections on or off.");
  setLiteral(11757, "A wall, window or door between source and listener. Damp = how much it");
  setLiteral(11758, "blocks (bass passes more), Open = how far the door or window is open,");
  setLiteral(11759, "Pos = where it stands, Back part = material of the room behind it.");
  setLiteral(11760, "Low cut removes everything below its frequency (rumble), high cut everything");
  setLiteral(11761, "above it (hiss). The dB value is the steepness per octave. Pre = filter the");
  setLiteral(11762, "input before source and room, Post = filter the finished output.");
  setLiteral(11763, "Levels in and out: In = gain into the plugin, Out = gain out of it,");
  setLiteral(11764, "Mix = balance between dry input and room. Limiter on: a look-ahead limiter");
  setLiteral(11765, "keeps every peak below \342\210\2221 dBFS (1.5 ms latency, compensated by REAPER).");
  setLiteral(11766, "What the room does to one short click: time runs left to right (ms), level");
  setLiteral(11767, "bottom to top (dB). Green bar = direct sound, blue bars = wall reflections,");
  setLiteral(11768, "shaded area = reverb tail. RT60 = time until the reverb has dropped by 60 dB.");
  setLiteral(11769, "%c");
